# Design

## Context

Stop reasons are written on paper and typed in later, if at all. The machines of the first implementation area already publish stop events through the IIoT Edge Platform; the data availability check found the stop event present and the reason missing.

## Goals / Non-Goals

**Goals:**
- Complete, event-linked stop reasons for the shift review.

**Non-Goals:**
- No maintenance work orders, no OEE calculation, no production planning. Growth beyond this is a new demand.

## Decisions

- **Route and sourcing:** 3a.3 external build under IT architecture guidelines (guided buy); no existing product covered the event link; the code stays with the company.
- **Hosting:** CMO with the standard manifests, deployed through GitOps.
- **Interfaces:** consumes machine stop events over MQTT from the edge platform; publishes to the data platform; no new proprietary interface.
- **Data model:** stop events and reasons in the agreed signal data model.
- **Cyber Security:** reuses the approved CMO platform pattern; pre-evaluation package attached.
- **Who runs it:** the building team runs it until IT formally accepts it.

## Risks / Trade-offs

- Operators skip the prompt under time pressure → the shift-end rule makes missing reasons visible instead of silent.
